	//   Let m = p-1, sum = s-x, upper bound = x-1 for each.
	//   Number = sum_{j=0}^{floor((s-x)/(x))} (-1)^j * C(m, j) * C(s-x - j*x + m - 1, m - 1)
	//   Wait, the upper bound is x-1, so we use inclusion-exclusion with "exceeding x-1" i.e. >= x.
	//   Number of solutions with each b_i <= x-1:
	//   = sum_{j=0}^{m} (-1)^j * C(m, j) * C(s-x - j*x + m - 1, m - 1)
	//   where C(n, k) = 0 if n < k or n < 0.

