	//
	// Actually, for a fixed x = a1, the condition for Hasan to have a chance is that all other players have score <= x.
	// Let M = max(a2, ..., ap). If M < x, then Hasan is the unique max, so he wins with probability 1.
	// If M = x, then there are (1 + number of players among 2..p with score x) players tied at the max, so Hasan wins with probability 1/(1 + count).
	//
	// This is getting complex. Let's think differently.
	//
